# --- generated artefacts -----------------------------------------------------
# Everything below is rebuilt deterministically from the committed corpus, the
# committed config and a recorded seed, so it is derived data, not source.
data/processed/clauses.jsonl
data/processed/index/
data/processed/probes/*/probes.jsonl
data/processed/checklists/*_draft.json

# Response logs are DELIBERATELY NOT ignored. They are the one artefact that
# cannot be regenerated — a probe comes back from a seed, a response is a
# purchase — and a few thousand of them is only a handful of megabytes. On an
# ephemeral machine, git is the backup. Losing this file means paying for the
# whole run again.
#   data/processed/runs/*/responses.jsonl   <- committed on purpose

# Deliberately NOT ignored, because they are provenance rather than output:
#   data/processed/checklists/*_signed.json  — the notary signature is the trust root
#   data/processed/probes/*/manifest.json    — seed, generator version, content hash

# --- model caches ------------------------------------------------------------
.cache/
models/
*.safetensors
*.bin
